map<int,vector<int>>mp

Think of map as a vector where the index/key can be almost anything.
Instead of:

v[0]
v[1]
v[2]
we can write:


mp[-2]
mp[-1]
mp[0]
mp[1]

So:

map<int, vector<int>> mp;

means:

For every int column, store a vector<int> of node values.

Example:

mp[-2].push_back(4);
mp[-1].push_back(2);
mp[0].push_back(1);
mp[0].push_back(5);
mp[1].push_back(3);

Internally, you can imagine:

mp

-2 -> [4]
-1 -> [2]
 0 -> [1,5]
 1 -> [3]

And the nice thing is: map automatically keeps its keys sorted.
